WEBVTT

00:05:28.864 --> 00:05:31.465
and it's the obvious things
that you can see.

00:05:31.489 --> 00:05:33.340
Someone got a promotion.

00:05:33.364 --> 00:05:36.198
"What are you doing, now?
What are you working on?"

00:05:36.222 --> 00:05:39.937
These are easy conversations --
easy-ish -- to have with people.

00:05:39.961 --> 00:05:41.652
The conversations around

00:05:41.676 --> 00:05:46.333
"Have you deepened your love
for your neighbor or your partner?"

00:05:46.357 --> 00:05:49.578
are much more intimate
and much harder to have.

00:05:49.602 --> 00:05:53.027
Do you see a risk that people
will shy away a bit and say,

00:05:53.051 --> 00:05:54.776
"I'm not ready for that"?

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.624
DB: No, you know, sometimes
I'm hired to give speeches

00:05:57.648 --> 00:05:59.684
at big convention halls
to corporate types,

00:05:59.708 --> 00:06:03.538
And so I'll walk into
a room with 4,000 people,